{"id": "clm:24610212d89007cd108dff60e0919228f832a0c27d6dfc8beca10270894d366e", "type": "statement", "text": "A FENS press release states that research presented at the FENS Forum 2026 compared post-mortem brain samples from 73 people with PD (28 women and 45 men) with 24 controls (9 women and 15 men). (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)", "source_url": "https://www.fens.org/news-activities/news/why-does-parkinsons-disease-affect-more-men-than-women-study-reveals-differences-in-gene-activity-in-the-brain", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Sex, age and ancestry differences and young-onset PD"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:21d2e23a34a50a9a1867effbb320e0fc3cff9a4d64bfe85e264dc256a0bdd4e1", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:07c6eb785b1b29e480d8b5354b8a02b52788d73a43ab66f6deecd758007c01ca", "ev:73685f41fb9607d745742c3074e6bc16e0b8d6d66f8412e2515af600f5e7b658", "ev:cead7d3b18023eedd843f232ecd7b76a99239b33949822b527a4e46d55639dc2"]}
